[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about wrong dates into one ticket and marked it
known, with one fix queued. The merge went by subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by tenant and by what each report
says, the ticket holds more than one problem. Each problem now has a ticket of its own.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix covers only the first problem. The other problems stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## The problems

**The parser reads every date month first.** Our tenants write the day first, so their dates
come out with day and month swapped: a booking for 7 April goes out as 4 July. This holds for
every channel except the booking-v3 form. It is the problem #4471 was named after.

**The booking-v3 form tells people to type the month first.** Its date field prints the hint
`MM/DD/YYYY`. The tenants on booking-v3 write the day first, so their people follow the
hint and type the month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way. The result looks like
the parser problem, a swapped day and month, but the cause is the hint. The parser fix does not
touch it. The #4471 page already shows this group as "no ticket of its own".

**Some bookings move by exactly one day.** "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday
11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." No day and month swap
in these: neither fix explains them. The desk had noted them as one-day moves and filed them
under the parser. The Lisbon and Toronto report points at time zones; that is a lead, not a
finding.

## How they were counted

- The ticket export pages overlap, so the same report can appear twice. Counted once per id.
- The cause comes from the tenant: where they are and which booking form they run
  (`src/lib/kb/causes.ts`). Not from the intake tag, which is a guess from the reporter's
  browser, and not from the subject line.
- The one-day moves come from the desk's own notes. Every report in #4471 was read to check
  that no other report describes a one-day move.
- The table above is computed from the export at render time (`src/lib/kb/problems.ts`).

## What follows

- Close #4471 as a merge of different problems; follow the tickets above instead.
- Merging on subject alone put these problems in one ticket. Decision 0001 should be replaced
  by a new record that merges reports by cause, not by subject.

